# What must not reach the build context.
#
# The context is sent to the daemon before the build starts, so a `node_modules`
# in it is tens of thousands of files transferred to be thrown away — the image
# installs its own, from the lockfile, inside the build.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Both are produced inside the build stage; copying the host's in
# would mean an image built from whatever the developer last compiled, which is
# the one thing a container build exists to avoid.
dist
**/dist
coverage
.vitest

# Runtime data, and whatever an operator's instance has accumulated.
# Anchored to the root on purpose. A bare `data` or `**/data` matches at every
# depth and silently excluded `apps/web/src/data/` — nine source files of the
# console's data layer — from the build context, so the image built an API whose
# frontend could not compile. Same trap as the `.gitignore` rule that hid the
# same directory from a clean clone; the fix is the same, and the anchor is the
# only thing that keeps it from coming back.
/data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.log

# Secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS and editor noise.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Documentation and design references are not needed to build, and `docs/` is
# several hundred kilobytes of Markdown that the build never reads.
docs
*.md
!README.md
